From 9cc862f2b8f6f134eedb6387c69aefca881cbf94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yeshihai <71063616+yeshihai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:18:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf][DSv4.1] Add opt-in candidate-only FP8 indexer decode
 on SM90

The V4.1 candidate-consuming indexers have no sparse scoring kernel on SM90, so they score the whole context and then mask down to the candidate blocks. Gather each candidate K from the paged FP8 indexer cache and score only the candidates with the existing non-paged kernel, then remap the selected columns back to request-local positions. The candidate-source and pre-candidate indexers stay dense.

Default off. Graph-aware path selection, small-batch protection and model-level accuracy are still open.
